<title>SPAIN: Telefonica and workers agree on 2.6 pct pay rise.</title>
<headline>Telefonica and workers agree on 2.6 pct pay rise.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Spain's Telefonica have agreed to a 2.6 annual pay rise this year, Telefonica said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Wage rises in 1998 will equal real inflation, and employees will be paid a 37,000 peseta bonus if productivity goals are met in each year.</p>
<p>Also agreed was a voluntary early retirement programme offered at 55 years old, the firm said.</p>
<p>The overall agreement reached with employees &quot;contains the tools which give the firm the strengths needed to guarantee competing in the liberalised telecommunications market,&quot; Telefonica said.</p>
<p>The deal includes overall measures aimed at improving operating efficiency.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
